430
01:04:01.730 --> 01:04:18.859
Anders Elowsson: And this EIP is very simple, it's just a one-time calibration of the fork boundary, where we add another constant so that we can change the cost per state part, and at the same time, normalize the limit of the gas, of the state gas.

431
01:04:19.330 --> 01:04:36.469
Anders Elowsson: So if we are in this situation where we create too little state bytes, we would instead reduce the cost per state byte, and at the same time, also reduce the limit, such that we can consume a correct amount of state bytes.

432
01:04:37.370 --> 01:04:57.230
Anders Elowsson: At the same time, if we are in this failure mode here, we will be increasing the cost per state byte, and at the same time, expanding the limit, such that we can consume more execution gas. And in practice, this is done by measuring the state gas used in normalized units.

